{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "The twelve-petal rose",
  "description": "The twelve-petal rose: the six-petal rose, a line straight up through 0, a second rose on the points that line and the first rose find, turned half a petal, and the hexagon through the first rose's points. Inside the hexagon the first rose's petals are red, the second's amber, each overlap of neighbouring petals amber, the rest blue.",
  "steps": [
    "A circle centered on 0, through 1.",
    "A circle centered on 1, through 0.",
    "Around the first circle, as for the six-petal rose: centered on the upper crossing, through 0.",
    "The next one around.",
    "The next.",
    "The next.",
    "The last. That is the first rose.",
    "A line from 0 straight up, through the point high above where two circles cross. It meets the first circle at the top and the bottom.",
    "A circle centered on the top point, through 0. It makes two new points on the first circle, halfway between the old ones.",
    "The same from the bottom point.",
    "Now go around again, on the new points: centered here, through 0.",
    "The next.",
    "The next.",
    "The last. A second rose, turned halfway between the petals of the first.",
    "The hexagon: from 1 to the next corner up.",
    "Across the top.",
    "Down the left.",
    "On down.",
    "Across the bottom.",
    "And back to 1."
  ],
